I would use "s" for both; however, in Spanish voicing is nondistinctive on=
=20
both phonemes /s/ and /=CE=B8/, so you could use "z" for either. I am not s=
ure if=20
there's any environment where [=C3=B0] can be an allophone of both /d/ and =
