since my accent uses /s/ for both "z" and "s".

As far as I can figure out, the Latin American dialects originated in=20
Andalusia, which shares both the leveling of /s/ and /=CE=B8/ (though in so=
me=20
Andalusian dialects they're both pronounced /=CE=B8/) and the disuse=20
of "vosotros".

I have proposed "zmase" for "enzima".

